---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import ClassRef from '../../components/ClassRef.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
import DsaScore from '../../components/DsaScore.astro';
import ApiTable from '../../components/ApiTable.astro';
import Demo from '../../components/Demo.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const demo = `<!-- Type a code and press Enter (a hardware scanner does exactly
     this, faster). data-scan-flash paints the viewport ok-wash on capture;
     REJECT* codes demo YOUR validation calling flashScanResult('error'). -->
<div class="bo-form-field">
  <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="scan-demo">Scan barcode</label>
  <input class="bo-input bo-input--code" id="scan-demo" data-scan-input data-scan-flash
      placeholder="Try 4006381333931, then REJECT-1" aria-describedby="scan-demo-status" />
  <p id="scan-demo-status" data-scan-status aria-live="polite" class="bo-visually-hidden"></p>
</div>`;

const canonical = `<input class="bo-input bo-input--code" data-scan-input data-scan-flash
    autofocus aria-describedby="scan-status" />
<p id="scan-status" data-scan-status aria-live="polite" class="bo-visually-hidden"></p>
<script type="module">
  import { initScanInput, flashScanResult } from "@busy-office/ui/js";
  initScanInput(); // capture -> ok flash (data-scan-flash) + live-region announce
  document.addEventListener("bo:scan", (e) => {
    // Capture is not validity. YOUR check decides, then paints the verdict:
    if (!isOnThisPo(e.detail.value)) flashScanResult("error", "Not on this PO");
  });
</script>`;
---
<Gallery title="Scan feedback">
  <p class="demo-note">
    The visible half of a barcode scan, for a user whose eyes are on the
    <em>rack</em>: a ~600ms viewport wash — green on capture, red when your
    validation rejects the code — paired, always, with the
    <code>data-scan-status</code> live region
    <a href={base + '/patterns/goods-receipt'}>the RF patterns</a> already
    link, so the cue is two-channel by construction. The device's beep and
    LED stay the device's job; this component never plays audio.
    <strong>Not for form validation on an ordinary screen</strong> — a
    seated user reading a form gets the field's own
    <a href={base + '/components/form'}>message</a> beside the control it
    concerns; a full-viewport flash there is noise aimed at nobody. Reach
    for this only when the user is physically away from the screen between
    inputs — which is the RF floor's whole context.
  </p>

  <section class="demo" data-density="spacious">
    <h2>Try it — capture flashes ok, your validation flashes error</h2>
    <Demo code={demo} />
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Capture ≠ validity: <code>data-scan-flash</code>
    makes the behavior paint <em>ok</em> the moment the terminator arrives
    (the scanner said "I read it"), and <code>flashScanResult('error',
    reason)</code> is your validation's verdict — the framework cannot know
    whether a perfectly-scanned code belongs on this PO. Under reduced
    motion the wash is static for the stamp's lifetime; under forced colors
    it becomes a Highlight frame, since a repainted background would vanish
    exactly when contrast matters most.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{canonical}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initScanInput, flashScanResult } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initScanInput();
    document.addEventListener('bo:scan', (e) => {
      const value = (e as CustomEvent).detail.value;
      if (/^REJECT/i.test(value)) flashScanResult('error', `Rejected: ${value}`);
    });
  </script>

    <section class="demo">
    <h2>What the platform gives you, and what the behavior adds</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Without <code>initScanInput()</code></th><th scope="col">What the behavior adds</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>A keyboard-wedge scanner types the code and sends Enter, so a plain input inside a form <strong>posts the scan</strong>. The screen still works</td><td>the <code>bo:scan</code> event, so a screen can react without a round trip</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Nothing announces the capture — the field just changes</td><td>the <code>[data-scan-status]</code> live region announcement</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No flash: the CSS keys off <code>data-scan-result</code>, which only the behavior stamps</td><td>the flash, and <code>flashScanResult()</code> for your verdict</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A trailing terminator character can land in the value</td><td><code>data-scan-terminator</code> stripping</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Unlike <a href={base + '/components/dialog'}>dialog</a>
    or <a href={base + '/components/combobox'}>combobox</a>, there is no native
    element underneath this one — a scanner is a keyboard, and the platform has
    no idea a scan happened. <strong>That makes the boundary more important
    here, not less</strong>: the no-JS path is a real form post and a server
    re-render, which every RF pattern page documents as its No-JS row. Build
    that path first and treat the flash as the enhancement it is.</p>
  </section>

<ClassRef component="scan" />
  <ApiTable
    component="scan"
    js="initScanInput() owns the moment: with data-scan-flash on the input, every capture stamps data-scan-result=&quot;ok&quot; on <body> for ~700ms (scan.css paints the wash; a timer clears the stamp, so the reduced-motion static wash cannot linger). flashScanResult(kind, message?) is exported for YOUR validation path — 'error' overrides a live ok, and a message lands in the [data-scan-status] live region."
    notes={[
      'Two-channel by contract: the wash is never the only signal — every capture and rejection also reaches the <code>data-scan-status</code> live region. That is the deliberate improvement over device-SDK overlays, which are colour-only.',
      'The overlay is pointer-inert and sits below toasts: a flash must never eat a tap or cover an error a consumer just raised.',
      'RF-profile member (its whole audience): counted inside rf-essentials\' 40 kB budget gate.',
      'No audio, ever — beeps and LEDs belong to the device service; pairing with them is configuration, not CSS.',
    ]}
  />
  <DsaScore component="scan" />
  <Related links={[
    ['/patterns/goods-receipt', 'RF goods receipt'],
    ['/patterns/rf-landing', 'RF task menu'],
    ['/components/state-patterns', 'Loading, empty & error states'],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
